Generally, when cutting thick plates and hot plates, the distance between the parts should be larger, because the heat influence of the thick plate and hot plate is greater. When cutting corners and small graphics, it is easy to burn the edges and affect the cutting quality.
In the process of cutting thicker plates, in order to make the seams good and prevent burns at the beginning and end, transition lines are usually introduced at the beginning and end of cutting, called lead and tail. Leads and tail are useless to the workpiece itself, so they should be placed outside the scope of the workpiece.
