High alumina bricks characterized with high thermal stability, high refractoriness above 1770 degrees, good slag resistance, mainly used for electric furnace top, shaft furnace, hot blast furnace, ladle, molten iron, cement kiln, glass kiln and other thermal furnace lining. Widely used in iron making, steel making, chemical industry, cement and other industries.
The thin slab casting and rolling process is a relatively compact and efficient new furnace technology, which is to cast 40-70 mm thin slabs with the continuous casting machine and after heat preservation or local heating, they are sent to the hot strip rolling mill to be directly rolled into 1.0-2.3 mm thick strips.
The inverted T-shaped castable prefabricated block structure allows the two end linings of the furnace cover to be buckled into the castable wall lining structure, so that the connecting parts form a labyrinth structure, which can achieve a good sealing effect.
