Cold stamping steels are mainly steel plates and steel strips, which account for 72.6% of the steel consumption of the whole vehicle. Cold stamping materials affect the quality, cost, output and production organization of products, so it is an important task to replace automobile stamping materials reasonably.
When selecting materials for automotive stamping parts, first select metal materials with different mechanical properties according to the type of automotive stamping and use characteristics. Generally, the following principles should be followed when selecting automotive stamping materials:
Most automobile compartment parts adopt roll forming process, which has certain requirements for material formability, rigidity, corrosion resistance and weldability. Generally, high-strength steel plates and ultra-fine grain steels with a strength level of 300-600MPa are used.
Frames, compartment plates and some important load-bearing parts are mostly formed by stamping molds, which require materials with higher strength and better plasticity, as well as fatigue durability, collision energy absorption capacity, and weldability. Generally, high-strength steel plates, ultra-fine grain steel plates (strength level of 300-610MPa) and ultra-high-strength plates (strength level of 610-1000MPa) with better formability are selected.
