According to the formula, the deformation of the tool and the length of the loading tool is the relation of the power of 3, the same diameter of the tool, when the long tool doubled, its deformation will increase 3 times.
It can be seen from the formula that the deformation of the tool and the diameter of the tool is the relationship of the fourth power, the same length of the tool, when the diameter of the tool is reduced twice, its deformation will increase by four times.
It can be seen from the above formula that the force (F) on the tool is proportional to the contact area (S) with the workpiece.Reduce the force on the tool by reducing the area of contact between the tool and the workpiece.
Use the tool path Angle function or the method of increasing the R position to reduce the load of the tool in the Angle position, so as to reduce the probability of the spring knife.
Conclusion: By comprehensively applying the three factors that affect tool deformation (tool loading length, tool diameter and cutting force), the probability of springing tool can be reduced, the processing time can be improved, and the machining accuracy and surface roughness can be better.
