More consistent color saturation from different viewing angles
If you are gaming a bit and want to relax and have fun in your free time or after work, these promises are mostly correct. Graphic designers love curved monitors because all color pixels reproduce the correct color value – from the center to the edge.
If you look at the marketing pages of curved monitor manufacturers, you might get the impression that curved screens relax and are easier on the eyes. So are flat screens harmful or even dangerous?
One study (source) states in the result that with eye pain, a curved monitor has noticeable positive effects compared to flat screens. However, apart from the fact that the study is anything but representative and thus meaningful with 20 test persons, the test participants did not notice any significant differences in headaches, dry eyes, tearing, or blurred vision.
I don’t know if this is a massive advantage in the battle of curved monitors vs. flat monitors, but – well, who needs light?
