Why Are There so Few Female Pro Gamers in Esport?
Nearly 50% of the female population in younger generations (and developed countries) play video games. Looking at local pro-gaming events, you will have to look for female pro gamers with a magnifying glass.
If you play Tetris on your mobile phone, you may be a video gamer, but you are very far away from Esport. Important games fairs such as E3 or the Gamescom show an equal number of both sexes visitors.
There are, however, more aspects that lead to this massive imbalance. Some are obvious; others are somewhat hidden.
