Anyone who has ever been to an NFL game knows the volume level in such a place. Even at esport events, the decibel level can soar so high that a team could no longer concentrate properly on the game.
Pro gamers must, therefore, always be able to hear 100% of the pure game sound. The superimposed headphones make this possible.
Many esport titles are much more complicated than football. The commentator explains everything in detail, from the characters, skills, and gameplays to the mostly unknown pro gamers.
If this information is known, it could be reacted to ad hoc. However, since the outer headset blocks all sounds from outside, viewers can get helpful information from the commentator.
An information advantage that a player gains by intentionally listening to the environment is called cheating.
Outside a noisy environment, it makes no sense to wear two headsets on top of each other. This is uncomfortable in the long run.
The headset helps to block out the last external noises in a reasonably quiet environment. The player can then also concentrate fully on the game sound in this version.
Communication is the most important part of pro gaming in a team. If we are very precise, we are not talking about two headphones, but one in-ear headphone and an ear-cup headset.
During these short activations, it can, of course, happen that the microphone also captures for a few seconds the external noise that the outer headset should actually block. This is accepted, however, because the information fragments are usually not usable by the players ad-hoc.
When in my professional career, my mousepad was dirty, I usually got a new mousepad sponsored.
When I recently noticed that my mousepad was quite dirty again, I didn’t do anything about it at first. Then, a few days later, my mouse sometimes felt sluggish, and when I moved it quickly, it wasn’t as precise as usual.
Are you using a mousepad made of hard plastic or even steel?
Hard surface mouse pads have enormous advantages when it comes to the procedure of cleaning. All you need is some warm water and microfiber fabric, and you can usually handle any dirt on your mousepad without any problems.
If your mousepad is very dirty, you can also use some alcohol (benzine or similar).
To protect the surface from scratches, you can also spray hard plastic mousepads with a silicone spray (a small drop, which is appropriately distributed, is enough).
If you belong to the large group of fabric mousepad users, it will be a bit more complicated. Still, it is usually more than worth the effort.
Therefore I recommend the following 5-step procedure:
Now, you take a sponge and rub the mousepad. If your mousepad is printed, you should not rub too hard because otherwise, the print could be damaged.
Then dry the mousepad with a clean fabric and let it air dry for at least 24 hours. It is crucial to make sure that the mousepad is completely dry before you use it again.
Therefore, you should plan for regular cleaning because the technology suffers, but on the other hand possibly also your health.
There were similar findings for the keyboards and mice used on them. This study showed that mouse pads have similarly high bacteria concentrations as keyboards, so you should probably clean your mousepad at least as often as your toilet.
Typically, you can also wash fabric mousepads in the washing machine. However, the manufacturer’s washing instructions must be followed to achieve the best result and avoid damage.
Otherwise, you can use regular detergent. If you have some in your household, you can put the mousepad in a separate net or laundry bag to protect it even more during the washing process.
Hopefully, you have not asked yourself if you can put the mousepad into the dryer…heat!!
We should start by unplugging the mousepad because electricity and water are the mothers of all bad ideas.
Wring out the cloth or sponge well to prevent uncontrolled water from flowing over the mousepad.
When you have cleaned everything so far, take your cloth or sponge and wash it out well so that there is no soap left on it. Then you can wipe the mousepad with it and wash the soap that is still on the mousepad bit by bit.
Of course, this cleaning is not quite as thorough, we have to make some sacrifices because of the electronics, but the drying phase does not take as long as with the more thorough cleaning method.
If the surface is damaged, the glide of the mouse suffers, and the mouse sensor could pick up incorrect position information. The use of bleach is therefore not recommended in any case.
Dirty mousepads are disgusting and have a negative impact on your performance as a gamer. Cleaning is quick, and the drying process of fabric mousepads can be done overnight.
Also, it will simply look better again.
