Unlike casual gamers, pro gamers must use all their skills and senses to make decisions that affect themselves and their team. Due to unique competitive gaming situations, pro gamers develop and train additional senses rarely used in casual gaming.
Top 5 Mechanics You Need to Master for Higher Ranking in FPS Games
FPS mechanics are the solid foundation for your success. But you can only make it to the top if you train the following skills (or senses) and constantly improve them.
How to Train These Skills?
Outstanding players can estimate how risky a revive is. If the teammate is knocked, then a Pro Gamer feels if the opportunity for a revive is there or if the fight has to be taken first.
Do you prefer to heal yourself first and then your teammate or vice versa?
It’s a combination of what a pro gamer sees, for example, an opponent running to the left and what the game situation dictates. In a Battle Royale game, the movement of the zone is a factor that influences the running paths of an opponent.
Pro gamers can make quick decisions when multiple enemies attack them or when the situation is changing quickly. Humans train processes to be able to call them up in extreme situations like a reflex without thinking.
This is an essential difference between casual and pro gamers.
Pro gamers have a good understanding of game mechanics that let them know how long it’ll take to reload a gun, how many bullets they have left, whether they’ll die if they go around an obstacle or not, etc. Often you see highlight videos on Youtube of your favorite game, where so-called IQ-moves are shown.
As a result, rational thinking is negatively influenced by feelings of stress. Wrong and hasty decisions are made, or they are executed imprecisely.
The process starts much earlier for a pro gamer. First, an opponent is seen.
Is the opponent alone, or is it a team?
Once that is clarified, then the opponent is targeted. Is the trigger pulled?
There are situations where it makes more sense to chase the opponent or wait until he gets involved in another fight. At the right moment, the fire is opened.
What is the opponent doing now?
