Masakari and I have been actively involved in improving games performance for more than 30 years. Whether Valorant should be played with or without one of these sync technologies interested us greatly.
We have analyzed over 1500 pro gamers. Here are the results for the best graphics card for FPS games.
VSync is an old technology for 60hz displays and should be turned off with modern monitors that can provide higher refresh rates (120hz, 144hz, 240hz, or 360hz). In addition, VSync is not compatible with other technologies like GSync or FreeSync and can lead to stuttering and increased in-game latency.
Finally, save all settings. If the setting also includes windowed mode and you notice problems with the next round of Valorant, NVIDIA recommends switching to fullscreen mode only.
Generally, Valorant is already optimized for the highest possible frame rates, and GSync only improves individual cases. The sync of refresh rates and frame rates causes input lag, which has a much more negative impact on performance than occasional screen tearing.
Generally, Valorant is already optimized for the highest possible frame rates, and FreeSync only brings an improvement in individual cases. In addition, the sync of refresh rates and frame rates causes input lag, which has a much more negative impact on performance than occasional screen tearing.
