Which Hobbies Are Totally Different?
The term includes all game genres, all platforms (PC, console, mobile), solo and multiplayer games, and online and offline games. Gaming can be divided into casual gaming and competitive gaming.
But a hobby remains a hobby, even if you act a little more ambitious, even if you earn a little from it. Only when you aim for a professional career in your hobby and want to make a living with it becomes serious.
The gaming industry is the fastest growing industry in the world. It is estimated that over 3 billion people play video games and can be considered casual gamers.
Gaming is becoming increasingly popular in every country in the world. The term casual gamer covers all people who regularly play video games, whether on a PC, console, or mobile device.
The spectrum of gamers ranges from housewives or househusbands to managers of large corporations. The gaming topic is still largely taboo in professional life, but as soon as people talk privately, gaming has become very important.
As soon as a person has access to a browser and the Internet, this hobby can be experienced directly. The entry-level is thus much lower than for other hobbies, where numerous and expensive pieces of equipment have to be purchased.
It has been scientifically proven that gaming can have a positive effect on psychological well-being. On average, casual gamers do not live unhealthier lives than non-gamers.
Scientific source 2.
It has been scientifically proven that multiplayer games played in teams can lead to strong social interactions and relationships. The intensive exchange about the hobby and playing together over a longer period are a good basis for friendships.
Of course, there are no upper limits. Someone who wants to install a computer in a real car for a racing simulator will have to shell out considerably more money than someone who buys a new mobile device for their favorite gaming app.
