Valve’s anti-cheat technology is integrated into almost 600 games on Valve’s Steam platform (2021). Here is the list of protected games.
Valve does not disclose what causes a VAC ban. Even the affected player only gets a message that a game ban has been initiated.
In general, a VAC ban only affects the game in which you applied the cheat. An exception is a VAC ban on a source game, which involves all related source games.
If VAC bans you, the corresponding account receives the following penalties:
You cannot receive VAC applied games as gifts
You cannot upload content on the Steam community for VAC applied games
According to Valves support Website, this statement applies: VAC bans are permanent, non-negotiable, and cannot be removed by Steam Support.
The pattern recognition of the VACnet technology can lead to an incorrect decision when evaluating detected software and scripts. If the wrong decision is reversed after a ban, the affected accounts are automatically unbanned.
