AMD works tirelessly to improve the graphics performance of their graphics cards, not only in the hardware area but also time and again in the software area. One of the latest developments is AMD FSR.
Which Graphics Cards And Video Games Support The Use of AMD FSR?
It is AMD’s counterpart technology to NVIDIA’s DLSS. However, the two work entirely differently from each other.
FSR’s technology comprises two parts, the first of which initially renders the game at a lower resolution and then scales it up. The second part of the technology then refines or sharpens the results.
The two different steps that AMD FSR uses for providing improved gameplay are as follows:
FSR uses spatial upscaling, the same technology that DLSS version 1.0 used, and the results were not very good. Therefore, the spatial upscaling got replaced by temporal upscaling in the second version of DLSS.
However, this sharpening pass is unique because it uses contrast adaptive sharpening.
The distinct pixel details make gameplay crisper and provide a more engaging experience.
Similar to NVIDIA’s DLSS, AMD FSR can also be easily activated in the respective graphics settings of the supporting games.
So, to see if FSR improves performance and frames per second, let’s look at case research on various titles and compare them to the native game without FSR.
This means that AMD FSR shows a considerable increase in the performance of various gaming titles.
The general thinking is that the extra effort put in by the AMD FSR will take more time to implement in real-world situations, so latency should be an issue. However, this is not the case.
In the case of FSR Quality, input latency has a value of 51.8, which is 12% better performance;
FSR Quality generates an input lag of 29.6, thereby resulting in an 18% performance increase;
FSR Performance results in an input lag of 24.5, a 33% increase in performance.
In addition to the games mentioned above, some of the titles that are likely to join the list of titles supported by AMD FSR include but are not limited to:
