Every gamer has undoubtedly stumbled across the FOV setting in a game, especially if you play a lot of FPS shooters. I have dealt with this issue a lot in my gaming career and tried out many different variations.
What Is the Impact of a High or Low FOV?
Where Can I Find a Good FOV Calculator?
In other words, Field of View refers to whatever I can see in front of me. If an object is closer to me, I need a larger angle to see it completely than if I am far away from it while observing the same thing.
FOV is subjective in the sense that it differs for each species of living being. Similarly, it varies from one device to another.
Field of View is significant in first-person shooter games because it determines which opponents I can see and thus interact with. The more I can see at a given point in time, the better because it allows me to make more informed decisions about the situation.
A wide field of view enables me to see more of my surroundings, but it also makes everything I see appear smaller. This is because when the FOV is increased in a video game, the overall screen size remains the same, but more information is displayed in the same area.
With a FOV of 60° in a first-person shooter game, I won’t be able to see nearby enemies who can easily shoot me. This is a common issue encountered by gamers who use this setting.
However, still, some people believe that the FOV value of 90° is the best for first-person shooter games as this setting offers the best of both worlds i.e. it not only allows us to see at greater distances but also gives us the ability to easily confront enemies located in close vicinity.
I know a lot of esports players that also use a 90° field of view. If these gamers are to survive in this cut-throat competition, they must be the finest, which suggests that 90° might be the best compromise for FPS games.
Further to that, many gamers do not follow the predefined standards and instead tweak the settings to find the number that is most comfortable for them. I’ve seen gamers pick random numbers like 93°, 96°, or 99° based on their choices.
You can read more about the importance of FPS in gaming here.
Although all of these FOV calculators provide some information to gamers, the result always seems to be dependent upon the personal preferences of gamers and their particular needs. After looking at a few of these calculators, I found that they all take different factors into account and end up presenting the user with a number that is not always comprehensible.
I came across a plethora of such FOV calculators, but the one presented by Sensitivity Converter is by far the best. The main reason behind it is that it takes into account additional factors, including the screen’s diagonal & vertical resolution, diagonal FOV, vertical FOV, and horizontal FOV, to come up with the best option for gamers.
FOV values don’t matter as much anywhere else as they do for shooter games because the right FOV can make or break the whole experience for players of such gaming titles. And because no converter currently exists that caters particularly to the needs of such gamers, or at least I couldn’t find one, I still believe that the slot for the best FOV converter is still awaiting its rightful owner.
For a real FPS shooter player, the FOV value is an essential setting, and unfortunately, there is no one answer to which FOV value you should set.
As a basic rule, however, the FOV should be as high as possible (to see as much of your surroundings as possible) and as low as necessary (the player models should still be large enough for you to see them quickly and to be able to aim at them without problems). Don’t worry.
