Can You Play CSGO With a Controller on a PC?
Does CSGO Have Aim Assist for Controllers?
Generally, CSGO can also be played with a supported controller on the PC, for example, a controller from PlayStation 4 and PlayStation 5 or Xbox. The game does not offer any functional aids (Aim Assist) to compensate for the disadvantages of controlling with a controller compared to other control options.
Technically, CSGO supports all controllers compatible with Windows 10. The button assignment of the controller can be freely selected.
Although CSGO generally supports controllers, there are no functional in-game control aids, such as Aim Assist, to support the use of a controller on the PC. CSGO is primarily specialized for the use of a mouse and keyboard.
In general, CSGO’s technical mechanisms are specialized for the use of a mouse and keyboard. The use of a controller is less precise and fast, for example, when flickshots and quick changes of direction need to be performed.
CSGO is optimized to use a mouse and keyboard. Some streamers have achieved good results on public servers with a graphics tablet, but they would be without a chance in competitive play.
Therefore, my explicit recommendation is to try it out, but you will see that CSGO is unplayable with a controller.
Apex Legends (APEX) is a popular first-person shooter video game that undoubtedly every FPS gamer tries out once. But, especially gamers who love to play on the console, ask themselves, is APEX also playable with a controller?
Is Upgrading Worth it?
An important change, especially for all left-handers, is the thumb buttons. The Logitech G Pro wireless is still universal, the buttons could be mounted on the left or right.
The mouse wheel has also been replaced with what I consider an even more stable variant, although I have to say that I already got along very well with the Logitech G Pro Wireless mouse wheel.
However, I have to say, the 16K Hero sensor was already excellent, and I can’t feel a difference from the new 25K Hero sensor. The second technical change is the battery, which is supposed to have a bit more power with 70 hours of battery life than the Logitech G Pro wireless, whose battery could offer a runtime of 60 hours (without RGB effects).
By the way, we’ve published an article on how you can restore your used mousepad to its former glory with a simple 5-step procedure. You can find the link at the end of this article.
A nice bonus is the Grip Tape, which is already cut for the mouse and is very easy to apply and of good quality. Since I tape every mouse with grip tape anyway, this is of course a useful accessory for me since I can save cutting the grip tape.
Universal (thumb keys can be mounted for left- and right-handed users)
The better glide is nice to have, but the Logitech G Pro wireless also glides smoothly. Everything else is more or less cosmetic, which also explains the still very high price of the Logitech G Pro wireless, as this mouse is also worth the money.
I recognized dirt on my mousepad but did nothing about it. Some days later, my mouse felt sometimes sluggish, and randomly it jumped on fast movements.
I have tried and tested many gaming mice in video games – including Rainbow Six . Furthermore, I know many competitive gamers who constantly wonder if their equipment is correct or worth buying a gaming mouse above $100.
In general, the Logitech G Pro Wireless is the best gaming mouse – not only for Rainbow Six. This mouse is also very popular with other first-person shooters.
Masakari has been successfully playing FPS Games at the highest level for over 20 years and is an experienced coach. So I asked him about the mechanics of shooters like Valorant, Call of Duty, PUBG or Rainbow Six.
Masakari and I have each been playing video games for over 35 years now. Especially in the FPS genre, an entire ecosystem of tools develops immediately after releasing a game to provide optimal support for competitive players.
That’s not just our opinion and experience, but that’s what Gaming Gear’s analysis of over 1700 pro gamers shows. We already wrote a post about it, the link of which you can find at the end of this post.
Final Thoughts on Curved Monitors for Playing Fortnite
An analysis of over 1700 Pro gamers with data from Prosettings.net shows that no single gamer currently uses a curved monitor. Instead, 100% of the gamers use flat screens.
Curved monitors make more sense than flat screens for many applications (Netflix ), but we are talking about first-person shooters here. For hand-eye coordination in Fornite, clear image quality plus low latencies during fast movements is the basis for a player’s performance.
When we have a new first-person shooter installed and start to look at the graphics settings, the same question has always come up for over 20 years: Anti-aliasing on or off. It was no different with Fortnite.
