7. The current situation does not conform to the pollutant discharge permit registration
* Whether to apply for the pollutant discharge permit in accordance with the law and discharge pollutants according to the content of the permit;
* Whether the construction project of the enterprise has fulfilled the EIA procedures and “three simultaneous” in accordance with law;
* Whether the site conditions of the enterprise are consistent with the contents of the EIA documents: focus on checking whether the nature of the project, production scale, location, production technology adopted, pollution control facilities, etc. are consistent with the EIA and approval documents;
Before a construction project is put into operation or use, its facilities for the prevention and control of environmental noise pollution must be checked and accepted in accordance with the standards and procedures prescribed by the State;If it fails to meet the requirements prescribed by the State, the construction project may not be put into production or use.
* Check whether the polluters have built new exhausts in areas where new exhausts are prohibited;
* Check whether there are sampling holes and sampling monitoring platforms on the exhaust gas pipe
* For unorganized emission points of toxic and harmful gases, dust and smoke, if conditions permit organized emission, check whether the pollutant discharging unit has carried out rectification and implemented organized emission;
* Waste gas collection should follow the principle of “collect all receivable and collect according to quality”.The exhaust gas collection system should be comprehensively designed according to gas properties, flow rate and other factors to ensure the exhaust gas collection effect.
* Waste gas should be collected by the gas collecting system of the production equipment itself as far as possible. When the escaping gas is collected by the gas collecting (dust) cover, it should be surrounded or close to the pollution source as far as possible to reduce the suction range and facilitate the capture and control of pollutants.
* The solid waste (hazardous waste) storage places with volatile organic materials or obvious odor should be closed, and the waste gas should be collected and treated and discharged.
Waste gas treatment * The production enterprises should select mature and reliable exhaust gas treatment process route after comprehensive analysis of the production amount of exhaust gas, the composition and nature of pollutants, temperature and pressure, etc.
* For medium concentration organic waste gas, adsorption technology should be adopted to recover organic solvents or thermal incineration technology after purification, discharge standards.
* Odor gas can be purified by microbial purification technology, low-temperature plasma technology, adsorption or absorption technology, thermal incineration technology, etc. After purification, it can be discharged up to the standard, and it will not affect the surrounding sensitive protection targets.
* Dust waste gas should be treated by a combination of bag dust removal, electrostatic dust removal or bag dust removal as the core.Industrial boilers and industrial furnaces give priority to clean energy and efficient purification process, and meet the emission reduction requirements of major pollutants.
* Check the rainwater and sewage diversion, and check whether the pollutant discharging unit implements the rainwater and sewage diversion.
* Cooling water is recycled through closed pipes;
* Enterprises entrusted with wastewater treatment should sign an agreement with qualified units, complete approval and transfer procedures, and set up a entrusted disposal account.
* In principle, each enterprise is only allowed to set up one sewage outlet and one rainwater outlet, and set up sampling monitoring Wells and signs.
* Units that meet the requirements of Article 4 of the Interim Measures for Supervision and Management of the Automatic Monitoring System of Industrial Pollution Sources in Jiangsu Province should install automatic monitoring equipment for discharge of major pollutants as required, and network with the monitoring center of the Environmental Protection Bureau.
