Cheerful fonts exist, and not because they contain a smile, but because their shape gives us a cheerful feeling. In graphic design, when we carry out a branding project for a certain brand or sector that maintains a more informal character, we can choose this type of font.
Round fonts, also called fonts rounded, They are part of the sans serif style and let's say that they are another of the styles that are part of what we know as typeface families. In this post, we are going to explain what they are and what functions they fulfill either by their design or their personality.
1 What are they and how did they come about?
In many historical writings this typeface is called Spanish Gothic, where the poems of Mio Cid were composed. Ultimately, this typographic style was so recognized that it began to be used in various teaching manuals during the Renaissance period.
Previously we have named you the Tironian notes, and it is that he was the main founder. This invention became official after the writing of the document made on December 5, in 64 BC, in which Cicero attacked Catilina with his words.
A typeface with a lot of personality
