And it is that Thomas Knoll, designed a program in Macintosh More during 1987, with which he sought to display grayscale images on monochrome screens. The following year and thanks to the help of his brother Knoll, he perfected what is now known as Photoshop, that is, a complete program with which different types of images can be edited.
The first two hundred copies of this program were distributed through the purchase of scanners in 1988 and it was in September 1989 that Adobe acquired Photoshop and then released it to the public in February 1990. Since then, Photoshop has not stopped renewing itself with each version through filters, plugins, tools, etc ...
Apart from adding new tools, options and improvements in each version that Photoshop released during all these years, also during 2013, Adobe made a bold change, causing a bit of controversy among its users by replacing the Photoshop payment model and changing the purchase of the license of each version, by the subscription model to Adobe Creative Cloud, either yearly or monthly. Currently, you must pay a monthly "rent" for each program separately or pay the entire pack.
