Poedit works by catalogs through which we can translate the terms that we deem appropriate.
Once we have done this we will configure our catalog by accessing the options from the menu Catalogue and setting Properties. Here we can modify several characteristics, although it will be enough for us to choose the language of our translation to Spanish and make sure that we work in a UTF-8 encoding.
When we have done this we can work with the translatable words and get to work. We will select each term and in the lower area a small window called Translation will appear, in which we will have to enter the corresponding one in the desired language, in this case in Spanish.
We will go to the language folder of our theme and choose the default language file to open it with Poedit. Generally, this file is usually called "default.po" or by following the name of the language with the format we have mentioned above (en_GB.po for example).
We will save our catalog assigning a naming format that we have seen previously in the languages folder of our theme and then we will get to work on translating the terms we deem appropriate. Of course when we finish we will save it again so that the information is updated.
We will open our application and from the menu Archive we will select the option New catalog from a POT file.
We will save our file following the language_COUNTRY naming format and we will begin to translate and then save and update the information again.
