Do you remember when we entered the world of handwritten fonts? Well then, get ready for another trip, because this time we are going to enter the world of round typefaces.
What are they and how did they come about?
Around the XNUMXth century, a new design of Gothic typefaces emerged in Italy, this is how the well-known rotund gothic.It had an extensive growth and development throughout the fourteenth century and at the time it received the name of round typeface. It receives the name of round because of the shape of the letters, since they are composed of marked curves and very open circles.
What most characterizes these fonts, despite their friendly and refined tone, is undoubtedly because they contain a large number of abbreviations that allow a great saving of the space between characters. This space received the name of tironian notes, founded by one of the greatest inventors of shorthand systems of the time.
Round fonts, before being what we know today, have had to go through a series of filters for their subsequent evolution. Most of these fonts not only come from Gothic writing but have had to be constantly designed, to be functional according to their time.
This typeface is used in a low box, since the lower case helps to reinforce its personality and appearance much more. To better understand this typographic style, we want you to imagine it as if it were a comedian or an animated character, where entertainment and creativity are most abundant.
