To: This is the path in which individual files are stored right after exporting.
Only visible layers: This is the box that tells Photoshop if users want each of the layers to be exported or if you only want to export those that are visible, that is, those layers that have the eye icon activated.
Include ICC profile: This is the option where you indicate if you want to include an ICC color profile in the exported layers.
Run: It is the option where the command is executed and also each layer is finally exported to the files.
Now that you know what the options available in the Export Layers feature towards files and what they are for, it is time for you to start putting it into practice.
If you follow these steps, you will export each of the icons that are in your document quite simply. Since this is about a very useful Photoshop function, which should undoubtedly be known and used by more people, because it offers the possibility of saving effort and time.
