The check valve is a type of valve used to protect against reverse flow, allowing flow only in one direction and preventing it from flowing in the opposite direction.
The valve is connected to the flange system on both sides.
When flow occurs to the valve, under the action of flow, the valve leaf is pushed out of the closed position and allows flow to pass through the valve. When the flow stops, the valve blade counters the backflow pressure and its own weight returns to the closed position, preventing backflow of water in the direction of the valve inlet.
Advantage: – Operation automatic based on the force of water flow, opening and closing quickly because the valve leaf is designed to tilt 45°.
– The valve is light in weight, compact in design, and takes up little space when installed.
