Water pollution is any chemical, physical or biological change in water quality that has adverse and destructive effects on the organisms that consume it. The concept of contaminated water refers to the accumulation and concentration of one or more substances other than water in the same to the extent that it causes an imbalance in biological life, human consumption, industry, agriculture, fishing and recreational activities and issues animals.
1.7 Chemical contamination of water
Surface water includes natural water found on the earth's surface, such as rivers, lakes, ponds, and oceans. These substances come into contact with water and dissolve or physically mix in it.
It is likely that this natural contamination cause serious human disease and the death of fish and other species. Pollution by suspended matter
These are called "particulate matter." These types of substances can damage or even kill aquatic organisms.
It is notorious to see how various industries use chemicals that are dumped directly into water sources. Agrochemicals used excessively in agriculture to control pests and diseases will eventually flow into rivers, poisoning aquatic organisms, extinguishing biodiversity and endangering human life.
Many times we say that water has healthy nutrition for living beings, so it is not necessary to decontaminate it. But the discovery of high concentrations of agricultural and industrial fertilizers in drinking water changed the whole situation.
Fertilizer runoff from farmland pollutes the water in rivers, streams, and lakes until it reaches the ocean. Fertilizers are rich in different nutrients necessary for plant life, and the fresh water produced changes the natural balance of essential nutrients for aquatic plants.
The sources of anthropic pollution that affect water quality are usually divided into two types:
Point sources of contamination: Point source of pollution refers to a pollution source that emits single or discrete pollutants in a single isolated or restricted geographic area. How to become: domestic wastewater discharge, industrial wastewater discharge, hazardous waste operations, mine drainage, leakage, accidental discharge, etc.
The same is true for acids, salts, and toxic metals. In high concentrations, they can cause serious damage to organisms, decrease in the yield of agricultural production and corrosion of work equipment.
They are soluble substances necessary for plant development and can stimulate the growth of algae and other organisms. This type of pollution can lead to eutrophication of water bodies, requiring the use of all the oxygen present.
1 What are solar collectors
Currently, in the solar market, we can distinguish the following types of solar collectors:
Solar collector with vacuum tube. This solar collector consists of a set of cylindrical tubes, made up of selective absorbers, located in the reflector seat and surrounded by a transparent glass cylinder.
It is usually made of glass, although plastic is also used because it is cheaper and easier to handle, but it must be a special plastic. Its function is to minimize losses due to convection and radiation, so it must have the highest possible solar transmittance.
Insulation layer: The purpose of the insulation layer is to cover the system to avoid and reduce losses. Because insulation is the best, the insulation material must have a low thermal conductivity to reduce the thermodynamic transfer of heat to the outside.
This water can be used as domestic hot water (80% integration), and can also be used to supplement the underfloor heating of the room (10% integration). Thermal solar panels can provide a large amount of hot water, But due to the instability of solar energy, they cannot completely replace the usual heating methods.
When defining and installing solar thermal installations, it must be taken into account that the solar collectors must be distributed in groups. These groups of solar collectors they should always be made up of units of the same model and distributed as evenly as possible.
I hope that with this information you can learn more about solar collectors and their characteristics.
